    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1145">

                <pb facs="0947" n="937" xml:id="pg937"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">119.2/2–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-14T13:00:00+08:00">February 14,
                            1949—1 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 14—4:04 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>515. No radio communications any kind ever transmitted behalf Chinese Government
                    over Mukden radio circuit (Peiping 192, February [8]). Complete file all traffic
                    held Shanghai control station.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 515; repeated Canton 56, Peiping 36, pouched Nanking 362.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
